# WF-005 – Workflow Policy Engine

**Document ID:** WF-005

**Title:** Workflow Policy Engine Specification

**Version:** 1.0

**Status:** Draft

**Owner:** S2PNexus Architecture Team

---

# 1. Purpose

The Workflow Policy Engine externalizes workflow behavior into reusable, metadata-driven policies.

Instead of embedding business rules directly into workflows, workflows reference one or more reusable policies.

This enables:

- Zero hardcoded business logic
- Reusable enterprise policies
- Simplified workflow maintenance
- Business-user configurability
- AI-assisted policy recommendations
- Cross-module policy reuse

---

# 2. Design Principles

The Policy Engine shall be:

- Metadata Driven
- Tenant Aware
- Version Controlled
- Reusable
- Extensible
- Auditable
- AI Ready
- Deterministic

---

# 3. Architecture

```
Workflow

        │

        ▼

Workflow Policy

        │

 ┌──────┼────────┬────────┬─────────┐

 ▼      ▼        ▼        ▼         ▼

Assignment

Escalation

Notification

SLA

Security

Policies
```

Policies are evaluated during workflow execution.

---

# 4. Policy Types

The Workflow Engine supports the following policy categories.

| Policy | Purpose |
|---------|----------|
| Assignment | Assign work |
| Escalation | Handle overdue work |
| SLA | Calculate deadlines |
| Notification | Send notifications |
| Security | Authorization |
| Approval | Approval routing |
| AI | AI execution |
| Retry | Retry strategy |
| Timer | Time-based execution |
| Validation | Runtime validation |

---

# 5. Policy Object

Every policy contains

| Field | Description |
|---------|------------|
| Policy ID | UUID |
| Name | Display Name |
| Description | Description |
| Policy Type | Assignment, SLA, etc |
| Version | Version |
| Status | Draft, Published |
| Tenant | Tenant Owner |
| Priority | Evaluation Order |

---

# 6. Policy Lifecycle

```
Draft

↓

Review

↓

Published

↓

Deprecated

↓

Archived
```

Published policies are immutable.

Rollback creates a new version.

